</p>
<p>The top right box contains games that should leave the collection. I&rsquo;m trying to figure out a system starting from the left (in) and ending to the right (out). The idea was also to have a few spaces on eye level where I could place the games that deserve more plays/attention.</p>
<p>So what&rsquo;s gone and what&rsquo;s new?</p>
<h2 id="the-gone-ones">The Gone Ones</h2>
<ul>
<li><em>Nightfall</em> was already &ldquo;culled&rdquo; in 2024 but I can&rsquo;t seem to make a sale on that one. It&rsquo;s out of print and I don&rsquo;t charge a lot. That is one persistent box!</li>
<li><em>Dungeons, Dice &amp; Danger</em> (Richard Garfield made a roll &amp; write and it&rsquo;s not very good)</li>
<li><em>French Quarter</em> is just not as good as <em>Three Sisters</em> and I can&rsquo;t justify owning both</li>
<li><em>Ora &amp; Labora</em> is the one that got felled as I own too many Uwe games and want even more</li>
<li>Speaking of which, <em>Click A Tree</em> is a disaster, I wish I didn&rsquo;t back that one.</li>
<li>I also gutted <em>Framework</em> and <em>Robin of Locksley</em> in 2025. Yes I have/had too many Uwe games, I told you. And <em>Nusfjord</em> is on my wishlist. Perhaps also <em>Hallertau</em>?</li>
<li><em>Conservas</em> is a neat little solo bag building game. I finished the campaign and it has not a lot of staying power after that.</li>
</ul>
<p>As mentioned in the 2024 post, we own too many small box 2-player only games that my wife no longer likes to play. <em>Glasgow</em>, <em>Caper</em>, and/or <em>Paris</em> are my next culling candidates.</p>
